Changes file for Speak

1.05    2026-09-10
        - Decoupled network transport logic from proprietary domains.
        - Made WAN server failover completely generic and configurable via
          SPEAK_WAN_SERVER, SPEAK_WAN_PORT, SPEAK_WAN_SCHEME environment variables
          and wan_server, wan_port, wan_scheme configuration keys.
        - Updated configuration search path order in Speak.pm (@CONFIG_PATHS).
        - Added persona setting to etc/speak.conf example configuration.

1.04    2026-08-27
        - Added logrotate configuration definition in etc/speak.logrotate for /var/log/speak.log.

1.03    2026-07-30
        - Adjusted the text-splitting algorithm in Speak::_split_text to respect
          word boundaries by splitting on whitespace instead of mid-word.

1.02    2026-07-27
        - Fixed speak() signature to make $log and $lang parameters optional
          (Perl feature 'signatures' enforces strict arity; previously calling
          speak($msg) with one argument caused a fatal error).
        - Fixed Speak::Logger::log() signature to make $nolinefeed optional.
        - Fixed stale $log->msg() call in mute-path logic (method was renamed
          to log() in a prior refactor, causing a fatal method-not-found error).

1.01    2026-02-06
        - Fixed issue where 'speak' script only read the first line of an input file.
        - Fixed pronunciation of escape sequences (literal \n, \t etc) by replacing them with spaces.

1.0     2026-01-11
        - Initial packaging of Speak.pm and its dependencies for CPAN.
